# The repository is already LF everywhere (git ls-files --eol confirms it), and
# Prettier is configured with endOfLine: lf. Without this file, core.autocrlf on
# Windows hands out CRLF on the next clone and every single file then reads as
# unformatted. Declaring it here keeps disk, index and Prettier telling the same
# story on any machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets, so Git never tries to translate line endings inside them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.svg text
*.webp binary
